# Two limits, one carbon-dioxide ledger
# Hold bicarbonate fixed while acid rises, then hold acid in excess while bicarbonate rises. Which reagent limits the computed carbon dioxide?
# Intermediate mission. Compare both four-vessel series: a larger dose raises
# the carbon ledger only until the other reactant becomes limiting.
#
# Model boundary: these are equilibrium inventory calculations, not a fizz-rate
# or bubble-volume prediction. The open virtual vessels can release carbon
# dioxide; foam height, nucleation, gas capture, heat exchange, mixing time and
# real preparation error are absent. A physical analogue should use small,
# teacher-prepared dilute portions, eye protection and an open vessel—never seal
# an acid/carbonate mixture.
register lv2
add v1 water 250mL
add v1 NaHCO3 0.004mol
add v1 HCl 0.0005mol
inspect v1
new
add v2 water 250mL
add v2 NaHCO3 0.004mol
add v2 HCl 0.001mol
inspect v2
new
add v3 water 250mL
add v3 NaHCO3 0.004mol
add v3 HCl 0.002mol
inspect v3
new
add v4 water 250mL
add v4 NaHCO3 0.004mol
add v4 HCl 0.003mol
inspect v4
new
add v5 water 250mL
add v5 NaHCO3 0.001mol
add v5 HCl 0.01mol
inspect v5
new
add v6 water 250mL
add v6 NaHCO3 0.002mol
add v6 HCl 0.01mol
inspect v6
new
add v7 water 250mL
add v7 NaHCO3 0.004mol
add v7 HCl 0.01mol
inspect v7
new
add v8 water 250mL
add v8 NaHCO3 0.008mol
add v8 HCl 0.01mol
inspect v8
